==English==

===Etymology===
Possibly a [[blend]] of {{term|splash}} and {{term|surge}}.<ref>[http://www.etymonline.com/index.php?search=splurge&searchmode=none Etymonline]</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/splɜː(ɹ)dʒ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-splurge.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)dʒ}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|splurg|ing}}

# To spend [[lavishly]] or [[extravagantly]], ''especially'' money.{{defdate|1934}}
#: ''They decided to '''splurge''' on the biggest banana split for dessert.''
#: ''The tomato sauce was '''splurged''' all over the chips.'' (British English)

